No it isn't.  The cursed wand will damage you slightly and blind you;
it's almost no effect.  Mojo can blow up your rings (conflict,
telecontrol, levitation, free action, whatever) and wands.  At that
point in the game, a small amount of ranged damage is much less
important than having a few outs (fire/teleport/wishing wands) in main
inventory.

So it's less _likely_ to have a negative effect, but the negative
effect it can have is very, very bad compared to almost meaningless
for the cursed wand (not to mention that most wands aren't cursed, and
uncursing them isn't a major problem).  Certainly having conflict on
is a major benefit to survivability (especially in the places where
survivability is really an issue) far greater than a few points of
Mojo damage, so "stash all your rings/wands" really doesn't seem like
a good play to me (except maybe for certain special circumstances
where you know the situation and can go ahead and prepare for it).

Besides which, if damage is really that important (almost never is to
a late-game valk) you should machine gun a stack of +7 daggers or
something.

